{"kind":"propose","text":"P1c bounded relay-profile direction: investigate and implement the proposed Noseq v0 reader policy as membership at the serving gateway's monotonically highest verified contiguous retained prefix, with a small membership-aware gateway in front of a network-private independently operated strfry backend. This is a deliberate availability-versus-revocation tradeoff for the prototype proposal, subject to full independent exact-head G5 review and later explicit profile adoption. It is not globally current authorization, a lease or a production deployment decision.\n\nI accept the following exposure for this bounded proposed-profile investigation, rather than infer it from the outage objective: if the mirror knows Bob admitted through prefix40 while removal41 exists only on an unreachable primary, Bob may retrieve previously unfetched old ciphertext, confidential-definition ciphertext and history metadata through40. Retained old keys/message openings may let him recover new-to-him old plaintext. Removal is not retroactive erasure; no claim that publication of an unseen removal instantly prevents mirror access. A newcomer admitted only at41 remains denied there. The mirror may serve no41+ bytes or closure using authorization40. This explicit exposure must remain visible in the proposed protocol, recovery/relay docs and adversary-by-asset table. It must not be summarized as current membership or strongest confidentiality. Final profile adoption must affirm this tradeoff again against reviewed evidence; this act does not adopt it for production.\n\nOnce the gateway verifies removal41, the removed subject is denied for all subsequent service output, including requests for40 and old pagination/subscription cursors. Persist the highest verified authorization frontier monotonically; apply controls before advancing any live output; hold suffixes with gaps/forks/half-controls. Recheck membership at dequeue/send boundaries, discard unsent queues, define bytes already released to the socket versus bytes newly authorized. An older requested data tip never rolls authorization back. Define policy when a verified newer revocation is learned before contiguous retention catches up; conservative denial is acceptable. Do not expose control/bootstrap history publicly to solve newcomer discovery.\n\nThe gateway must independently verify the owner/public-admission/genesis/accepted-boundary binding fixed by G3 and AUTH's connection, exact endpoint and key possession. AUTH itself grants no membership. Trusted operators/control replication may see declared metadata; operators have no decrypt or recovery keys. Keep private ingestion/replication separate from public reader APIs and make backend bypasses unreachable by deployment contract, with local real isolation fixtures where claimed. Deny COUNT/HLL/NEG, broad/cross-instance/disjunctive bypass filters, raw passthrough, export and administration on the public surface. Advertise only actual gateway NIPs/limits. Preserve normal retained history and explicit NIP70 publication/replication treatment.\n\nSelect full newcomer application history as the G2 proposal already under implementation, with exact authenticated interval, original ciphertext/action/definition verification closure and explicit owner-attested control-transition interval. Distinguish publicly verified transport authorization from this owner-attested recovery trust. Primary-outage recovery works only through the mirror's named retained complete prefix; no freshness/completeness claim beyond it. Full closure missing at a named tip is partial/unavailable, never EOSE-as-complete.\n\nRollback/restore: distinguish ordinary restart with intact durable monotonic state from restoring an old database or losing the authoritative state. A restore must remain read-disabled until it reconciles an external trusted high-water mark/removal state; a local backup cannot prove absence of a forgotten later removal. This may prevent recovery during an authority outage after restore. Do not fake a currentness guarantee with a signed-but-stale tip. P5 must prove actual durable restore fencing; P1c must define and exercise the isolated state machine without claiming production persistence.\n\nImplement the smallest isolated executable gateway/policy fixtures needed to establish G5 feasibility under the live P1c request, preserving its ownership and allowed development-only scope. Use the reviewed assessment's F01-F08 cases as coverage obligations with honest executed/unexecuted labels. Real bounded local gateway/strfry probes are permitted; do not integrate production primary/mirror services, deploy, open external ports or install globally. Keep Plan001's resource targets unless an explicitly justified reviewed adjustment is necessary; reviewer example values are not adopted defaults. Bind native source/binary/build/script/config/probe evidence exactly, retaining failures. A model of ACL decisions alone is not proof of actual socket/filter/history/live paths. G5 and full gates remain pending until the required proposed-profile evidence and actual independent review decisions validate.\n\nStrict globally-current fail-closed service and strict-current-plus-outage service remain documented alternatives, not a second implemented mode. The latter requires an independent authority or serving-set revocation/fencing barrier, with corresponding availability/coordination cost. Do not add that general framework to this prototype without a separate decision.\n\nThis direction refines the live P1c investigation request ac4cde53ea4a93e1ac8ef372524d78de64e37c39, without a duplicate commitment or permission to bypass its two-day checkpoint, security STOP conditions, all-path independent review, actual review/adoption records, closed full gates, or separate P2-P9 requests. Basis: live Plan001 and landed crypto artifacts; completed assessment389f159594d1dda04bc6e5b75436b788544eda21 and supplement9d9af3e02419988ac3d82fbfd79d22cd3f1dd2df were requester-ratified. Native observations30cffe8f2edd437f3b784b0a9415e5bb40a3b6ca and builder checkpoint9136fd7a6335e9e8c2096128bdcc2269437f545c are evidence of local observations, not gate passes.","body":{"exposure":"unseen removal may permit old-history retrieval through the mirror frontier","policy":"membership-at-highest-verified-retained-prefix","scope":"P1c proposed profile and isolated feasibility only; no production adoption"}}